WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.485 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Where could floodwater go along
the Gandak River in Bihar?

00:00:04.766 --> 00:00:07.817 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
TerraScope lets us look
for places worth surveying.

00:00:10.399 --> 00:00:14.083 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
First, let's go back
to September 28, 2024.

00:00:14.782 --> 00:00:18.056 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
By October 2, the modeled
river flow has changed.

00:00:18.754 --> 00:00:22.800 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The replay lets you follow rainfall
and river flow side by side.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.206 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Now let’s zoom in near Sonepur.

00:00:25.906 --> 00:00:28.805 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The map picks out low spots
in the surrounding terrain.

00:00:29.505 --> 00:00:31.798 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Those give a field
team a place to start.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.080 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Open a candidate and you
can see its footprint.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.273 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The map estimates how much water
would fill it up to the spill rim.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:43.774 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
How much could actually be
stored there is still unknown.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.879 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The terrain profile shows the dip
and where water might spill.

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:53.448 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
A field team can use it to plan where
to check the outlet and drainage.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.563 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
A student built TerraScope and
asked an AI agent to publish it.

00:01:00.263 --> 00:01:02.645 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The prompt you see here
is a reconstruction.

00:01:03.345 --> 00:01:07.513 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
The agent deployed the app with Embarko,
so anyone can open the map.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.130 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
You can try TerraScope
at the address on screen.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:16.498 line:73% position:50% size:80% align:center
Replay the storm and pick a site
you'd want to look at more closely.
